# Education loan — hidden from UI, kept in code

The education loan product is **not shown** on the public Shroffin website right now. Home loans are the focus of the redesign.

## Always

1. **Do not** add education loan links, CTAs, nav items, banners, or marketing copy to customer-facing UI (especially `index.html` and redesigned pages).
2. **Do not delete** education loan code or pages — keep them in the repo for later.
3. When removing education loan from the UI, **comment it out** or gate it with a clear marker (`EDUCATION_LOAN_PRODUCT` / `LEGACY_EDUCATION_PAGES`), instead of deleting.
4. Files to preserve (non-exhaustive): `education-loan.html`, `table-embed.html`, related `pages/*` loan flows, `js/compare.js`, `js/aoo-loan-table-standalone.js`, sheet/config code for education loans.
5. Redesigned home nav must not link to legacy education loan pages (`compare`, `quick-overview`, `schemes`, `faq`, `document-checklist`, `about` as currently written, or `education-loan.html`) until those pages are rebuilt for the current product or the user re-enables education loans.

## Never

- Do not link `education-loan.html` from the home nav or home page until the user explicitly re-enables the product.
- Do not rewrite or remove education loan internals “to clean up” without an explicit ask.
- Do not surface “Education” as a product in the redesigned global nav.

## Re-enable later

Uncomment blocks marked `EDUCATION_LOAN_PRODUCT` (and restore any gated links) only when the user asks to show education loans again.
